{"strongs": "H2850", "word": "חִתִּי", "translit": "chit.ti", "root": "חת", "morph": "N:N--PG", "pos": "adjective", "gloss": "Hittite(s)", "definition": "חִתִּי adjective and name, of a people Hittite(s) (Egyptian –-tá, –etá W Max Müll Asien u. Europa, 319 ff. ; Assyrian –atti , Schr KG 192 ff. COT on Gen 10:19 Dl Pa, 269 ff. ; Tel el-Amarna –atti, –atta Bez Tel el Amarn. Brit. Mus. 150 ) — masculine always with article הַחִתִּי Gen 23:10 ; Exod 3:8 +; feminine חִתִּית Ezek 16:3 ; Ezek 16:45 masculine plural הַחִתִּים Josh 1:4 + 3 t.; feminine plural חִתִּיֹּת 1Kgs 11:1 — 1. adjective , of seller of Machpelah to Abraham, עֶפְרוֺן הַחִתִּי Gen 23:10 ; Gen 49:29 ; Gen 49:30 ; Gen 50:13 עֶפְרֹן בֶּןצֹֿחַר ׳ הַח Gen 25:9 (all P ); of fathers of Esau's wives בְּאֵרִי ׳ הַח Gen 26:34 ׳ אֵילוֺן הַח v Gen 26:34 ; Gen 36:2 (all P ); also of warriors of David, ׳ אֲחִימֶלֶךְ הַח 1Sam 26:6 , and especially ׳ אוּרִיָּה הַח 2Sam 11:3 ; 2Sam 11:6 ; 2Sam 11:17 ; 2Sam 11:21 ; 2Sam 11:24 ; 2Sam 12:9 ; 2Sam 12:10 ; 2Sam 23:39 ; 1Kgs 15:5 ; 1Chr 11:41 feminine singular = substantive, only of (religious) ancestry of Jerusalem Ezek 16:3 thy father was the Amorite, and thy mother was a Hittite woman חִתִּית , similarly v Ezek 16:45 feminine plural = substantive of Solomon's foreign wives, חִתִּיֹּת 1Kgs 11:1 Hittite women (+ מוֺאֲבִיּוֺת , עַמּוֺנִיּוֺת , אֲדֹמִיֹּת , צֵדְנִיֹּת ). 2. n. usually \\ \\ a. collective הַחִתִּי the Hittites: in lists of Canaanitish peoples Gen 15:20 ( J E ), Exod 3:8 ; Exod 3:11 (both J ), Exod 13:5 ; Exod 23:23 ; Exod 23:28 ; Exod 33:2 ; Exod 34:11 ; Num 13:29 ; Josh 3:10 (all J E ), Deut 7:1 ; Deut 20:17 ; Josh 9:1 ; Josh 12:8 ; Josh 24:11 (all D ); read also for הַחִוִּי Judg 3:3 (so We Mey Bu Urg 350 ); in Josh 11:3 ( D ) strike out הַחִתִּי We Mey Bu l.c. , and read then הַחִתִּי for הַחִוִּי v b (so ᵐ5 , not ᵐ5 L ); further 1Kgs 9:20 = 2Chr 8:7 ; Ezra 9:1 ; Neh 9:8 . \\ \\ b. plural ׃הַחִתִּים כֹּל אֶרֶץ הַחִתִּים Josh 1:4 ( D ) nearly = land of Canaanites; ׳ ארץ הַח specifically of northern home of Hittites Judg 1:26 so also 2Sam 24:6 where read אֶרֶץ הַחִתִּים קֵ֫דְשָׁה (for ᵑ0 תחתים חָדְשִׁי , see חָדְשִׁי , קֵדֶשׁ ); מַלְכֵי הַחִתִּים 1Kgs 10:29 = 2Chr 1:17 (both + מַלְכֵי אֲרָם ), 2Kgs 7:6 (+ מַלְכֵי מִצְרַיִם , both feared by אֲרָם ). Hence it appears that הַחִתִּי (םׅ had their proper seat in the north — where also they were encountered by Assyrians from time of Tiglath-Pileser I (see Schr Dl 1. c .), and by Egyptians from time of Tutmes III (see W Max Müll. l.c. ) — (compare also Judg 3:3 ; Josh 11:3 above), but that individual Hittites were known in Israel (compare, besides 1Sam 2:6 ; 2Sam 11:3 etc., 1Kgs 9:20 above); that the Hittites were regarded (by J E D ) as one of the peoples of Canaan, and that the name even came to be used in more general sense for Canaanites. Only in P do they appear as having a definite settlement in the south, and are designated by בְּנֵיחֵֿת (see חֵת ), as well as by the adjective הַחִתִּי .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3242')\">BDB3242</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H2850')\">H2850</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3241')\">BDB3241</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3243')\">BDB3243</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>חִתִּי</bdbheb> <b>adjective</b> and <b>name, of a people</b> <highlightword>Hittite(s)</highlightword> (Egyptian <transliteration><highlight>–-tá, –etá</highlight></transliteration> W Max <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('WMM')\">Müll<sup>Asien u. Europa, 319 ff.</sup></lookup>; Assyrian <transliteration><highlight>–atti</highlight></transliteration>, <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Schr')\">Schr<sup>KG 192 ff.</sup></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('COT')\">COT</lookup> on <ref ref=\"Gen 10:19\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(1,10,19)\">Gen 10:19</ref> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Dl')\">Dl<sup>Pa, 269 ff.</sup></lookup>; Tel el-Amarna <transliteration><highlight>–atti, –atta</highlight></transliteration> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Bez')\">Bez<sup>Tel el Amarn. Brit. Mus. 150</sup></lookup>) — masculine always with article <bdbheb>הַחִתִּי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 23:10\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(1,23,10)\">Gen 23:10</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 3:8\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(2,3,8)\">Exod 3:8</ref> +; feminine <bdbheb>חִתִּית</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 16:3\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(26,16,3)\">Ezek 16:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 16:45\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"45\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"45\" onclick=\"bcv(26,16,45)\">Ezek 16:45</ref> masculine plural <bdbheb>הַחִתִּים</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Josh 1:4\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(6,1,4)\">Josh 1:4</ref> + 3 t.; feminine plural <bdbheb>חִתִּיֹּת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Kgs 11:1\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(11,11,1)\">1Kgs 11:1</ref> — <div class=\"point\"><b>1. adjective </b>, of seller of Machpelah to Abraham, <bdbheb>עֶפְרוֺן הַחִתִּי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 23:10\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(1,23,10)\">Gen 23:10</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 49:29\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"49\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"49\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(1,49,29)\">Gen 49:29</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 49:30\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"49\" vBegin=\"30\" cEnd=\"49\" vEnd=\"30\" onclick=\"bcv(1,49,30)\">Gen 49:30</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 50:13\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"50\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"50\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(1,50,13)\">Gen 50:13</ref> <bdbheb>עֶפְרֹן בֶּןצֹֿחַר</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>הַח</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 25:9\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"25\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"25\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(1,25,9)\">Gen 25:9</ref> (all <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('P')\"><reflink>P</reflink></lookup>); of fathers of Esau's wives <bdbheb>בְּאֵרִי</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>הַח</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 26:34\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"26\" vBegin=\"34\" cEnd=\"26\" vEnd=\"34\" onclick=\"bcv(1,26,34)\">Gen 26:34</ref> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>אֵילוֺן הַח</bdbheb> v<ref ref=\"Gen 26:34\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"26\" vBegin=\"34\" cEnd=\"26\" vEnd=\"34\" onclick=\"bcv(1,26,34)\">Gen 26:34</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 36:2\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"36\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"36\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(1,36,2)\">Gen 36:2</ref> (all <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('P')\"><reflink>P</reflink></lookup>); also of warriors of David, <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>אֲחִימֶלֶךְ הַח</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Sam 26:6\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"26\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"26\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(9,26,6)\">1Sam 26:6</ref>, and especially <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>אוּרִיָּה הַח</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"2Sam 11:3\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(10,11,3)\">2Sam 11:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Sam 11:6\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(10,11,6)\">2Sam 11:6</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Sam 11:17\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(10,11,17)\">2Sam 11:17</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Sam 11:21\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(10,11,21)\">2Sam 11:21</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Sam 11:24\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"24\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"24\" onclick=\"bcv(10,11,24)\">2Sam 11:24</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Sam 12:9\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(10,12,9)\">2Sam 12:9</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Sam 12:10\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(10,12,10)\">2Sam 12:10</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Sam 23:39\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"39\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"39\" onclick=\"bcv(10,23,39)\">2Sam 23:39</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Kgs 15:5\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(11,15,5)\">1Kgs 15:5</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Chr 11:41\" b=\"13\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"41\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"41\" onclick=\"bcv(13,11,41)\">1Chr 11:41</ref> feminine singular = substantive, only of (religious) ancestry of Jerusalem <ref ref=\"Ezek 16:3\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(26,16,3)\">Ezek 16:3</ref> <highlight>thy father was the Amorite, and thy mother was a Hittite woman</highlight> <bdbheb>חִתִּית</bdbheb>, similarly v<ref ref=\"Ezek 16:45\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"45\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"45\" onclick=\"bcv(26,16,45)\">Ezek 16:45</ref> feminine plural = substantive of Solomon's foreign wives, <bdbheb>חִתִּיֹּת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Kgs 11:1\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(11,11,1)\">1Kgs 11:1</ref> <highlight>Hittite women</highlight> (+ <bdbheb>מוֺאֲבִיּוֺת</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>עַמּוֺנִיּוֺת</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>אֲדֹמִיֹּת</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>צֵדְנִיֹּת</bdbheb>). </div><div class=\"point\"><b>2. n.</b> usually <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>a.</b> collective <bdbheb>הַחִתִּי</bdbheb> <highlight>the Hittites:</highlight> in lists of Canaanitish peoples <ref ref=\"Gen 15:20\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(1,15,20)\">Gen 15:20</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup><lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('E')\"><reflink>E</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Exod 3:8\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(2,3,8)\">Exod 3:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 3:11\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(2,3,11)\">Exod 3:11</ref> (both <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Exod 13:5\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(2,13,5)\">Exod 13:5</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 23:23\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(2,23,23)\">Exod 23:23</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 23:28\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"28\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"28\" onclick=\"bcv(2,23,28)\">Exod 23:28</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 33:2\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"33\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"33\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(2,33,2)\">Exod 33:2</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 34:11\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"34\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"34\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(2,34,11)\">Exod 34:11</ref>; <ref ref=\"Num 13:29\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(4,13,29)\">Num 13:29</ref>; <ref ref=\"Josh 3:10\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(6,3,10)\">Josh 3:10</ref> (all <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('E')\"><reflink>E</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Deut 7:1\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(5,7,1)\">Deut 7:1</ref>; <ref ref=\"Deut 20:17\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(5,20,17)\">Deut 20:17</ref>; <ref ref=\"Josh 9:1\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(6,9,1)\">Josh 9:1</ref>; <ref ref=\"Josh 12:8\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(6,12,8)\">Josh 12:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"Josh 24:11\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(6,24,11)\">Josh 24:11</ref> (all <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('D')\"><reflink>D</reflink></lookup>); read also for <bdbheb>הַחִוִּי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Judg 3:3\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(7,3,3)\">Judg 3:3</ref> (so <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('We')\">We</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Mey')\">Mey</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Bu')\">Bu<sup>Urg 350</sup></lookup>); in <ref ref=\"Josh 11:3\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(6,11,3)\">Josh 11:3</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('D')\"><reflink>D</reflink></lookup>) strike out <bdbheb>הַחִתִּי</bdbheb> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('We')\">We</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Mey')\">Mey</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Bu')\">Bu<sup>l.c.</sup></lookup>, and read then <bdbheb>הַחִתִּי</bdbheb> for <bdbheb>הַחִוִּי</bdbheb> v<sup>b</sup> (so <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup>, not <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb><sup><reflink>L</reflink></sup></lookup>); further <ref ref=\"1Kgs 9:20\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(11,9,20)\">1Kgs 9:20</ref> = <ref ref=\"2Chr 8:7\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(14,8,7)\">2Chr 8:7</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezra 9:1\" b=\"15\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(15,9,1)\">Ezra 9:1</ref>; <ref ref=\"Neh 9:8\" b=\"16\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(16,9,8)\">Neh 9:8</ref>. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>b.</b> plural <bdbheb>׃הַחִתִּים</bdbheb> <bdbheb>כֹּל אֶרֶץ הַחִתִּים</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Josh 1:4\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(6,1,4)\">Josh 1:4</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('D')\"><reflink>D</reflink></lookup>) nearly = land of Canaanites; <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ארץ הַח</bdbheb> specifically of northern home of Hittites <ref ref=\"Judg 1:26\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"26\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"26\" onclick=\"bcv(7,1,26)\">Judg 1:26</ref> so also <ref ref=\"2Sam 24:6\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(10,24,6)\">2Sam 24:6</ref> where read <bdbheb>אֶרֶץ הַחִתִּים קֵ֫דְשָׁה</bdbheb> (for <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('MT')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ0</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <bdbheb>תחתים חָדְשִׁי</bdbheb>, see  <bdbheb><reflink>חָדְשִׁי</reflink></bdbheb>, <bdbheb>קֵדֶשׁ</bdbheb>); <bdbheb>מַלְכֵי הַחִתִּים</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Kgs 10:29\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(11,10,29)\">1Kgs 10:29</ref> = <ref ref=\"2Chr 1:17\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(14,1,17)\">2Chr 1:17</ref> (both + <bdbheb>מַלְכֵי אֲרָם</bdbheb>), <ref ref=\"2Kgs 7:6\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(12,7,6)\">2Kgs 7:6</ref> (+ <bdbheb>מַלְכֵי מִצְרַיִם</bdbheb>, both feared by <bdbheb>אֲרָם</bdbheb>). Hence it appears that <bdbheb>הַחִתִּי (םׅ</bdbheb> had their proper seat in the north — where also they were encountered by Assyrians from time of Tiglath-Pileser I (see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Schr')\">Schr<sup></sup></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Dl')\">Dl<sup>1. c</sup></lookup>.), and by Egyptians from time of Tutmes III (see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('WMM')\">W Max Müll.<sup>l.c.</sup></lookup>) — (compare also <ref ref=\"Judg 3:3\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(7,3,3)\">Judg 3:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"Josh 11:3\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(6,11,3)\">Josh 11:3</ref> above), but that individual Hittites were known in Israel (compare, besides <ref ref=\"1Sam 2:6\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(9,2,6)\">1Sam 2:6</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Sam 11:3\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(10,11,3)\">2Sam 11:3</ref> etc., <ref ref=\"1Kgs 9:20\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(11,9,20)\">1Kgs 9:20</ref> above); that the Hittites were regarded (by <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('E')\"><reflink>E</reflink></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('D')\"><reflink>D</reflink></lookup>) as one of the peoples of Canaan, and that the name even came to be used in more general sense for Canaanites. Only in <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('P')\"><reflink>P</reflink></lookup> do they appear as having a definite settlement in the south, and are designated by <bdbheb>בְּנֵיחֵֿת</bdbheb> (see  <bdbheb><reflink>חֵת</reflink></bdbheb>), as well as by the adjective <bdbheb>הַחִתִּי</bdbheb>. </p></div><hr>", "references": [{"raw": "Gen 10:19", "book": "GEN", "chapter": 10, "verse":